  "plot_summary": "[HANG0 ] As expected, the results of the \"Can we drop the letters page from Spider-Man?\" survey are announced, and to no one's surprise, Marvel realized that [SPAN: severity=info; text=readers overwhelmingly <i>demanded</i> they keep it.]&nbsp; They concluded with:&nbsp; <i>if Spidey can learn to climb walls, maybe we can learn to go without sleep!</i>\"\n[BR]\n[BR] This may actually be the first time Marvel has referred to Spider-Man as \"[SPAN: severity=info; text=Spidey].\"&nbsp; It's a nickname that ultimately comes into general use, but this is the first time I remember seeing the editors actually <i>use</i> the term.&nbsp; Note, though, that [SPAN: severity=warning; text=it still has not appeared anywhere in the book's actual narrative,] so until it does, I have been careful not to use it in any plot summaries or reviews.\n\n[HANG0] The next issues of both <i>Avengers</i> and <i>X-Men</i> are announced (issue 4 in both cases) as going on sale on January 3, 1964.&nbsp; This turns out to be true.&nbsp; But it also promises that the next issue of <i>Fantastic Four</i> is on sale on that date, which is <i>not</i> true (it was published one week later).\n\n[HANG0] The return of Captain America is announced (based on reader demand), which will take place in <i>Avengers</i> 4 (AVEN #4).",
